## 4. Low-Level Hardware & Overclocking Disclaimer
CurveSmith executes low-level kernel driver calls (Ring-0) to modify AMD Ryzen SMU tables, Curve Optimizer voltage offsets, telemetry flags, and core clock frequencies. 

By executing this software, you expressly acknowledge and agree that:
- Operating hardware components outside factory specifications, recommended voltage boundaries, or default boost ceilings may permanently void processor and motherboard warranties.
- Adjusting voltage curves, dynamic offsets, or static frequencies carries inherent physical risks, including but not limited to: accelerated silicon degradation, thermal throttling, permanent hardware damage (CPU/motherboard burnout), power supply trigger trips, operating system corruption, sudden system crashes (BSOD), and irreversible data loss.
- Silicon quality varies per sample. Frequencies or negative Curve Optimizer offsets that are stable on one processor may cause immediate instability or hardware failure on another.

